    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-subgraph-layout.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the convention comes from",
      "prov:value": "The \"giant diagram\" is the **i2ce Form Documentor**:\n`I2CE_Page_FormDocumentor::dot()` in i2ce 4.3.3\n(`i2ce/modules/Forms/modules/FormDocumentor`). It wrote every form of an iHRIS\nsite as Graphviz DOT and piped it through `unflatten -f -l 2 -c 2 | dot`. A\nfolio that holds the iHRIS forms restated it over a projection so any subgraph\ncould be drawn with it, and this platform skill generalizes that again: the\nprojection here is the UML overview's own model, so the drawing is of a\nharness's KG declaration schema rather than of forms."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-subgraph-layout.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the convention comes from",
      "prov:value": "- **A node is a rounded box whose label is a table**: a header, then one row\n  per property. The Form Documentor declared `shape=\"Mrecord\"`; here the shape\n  is `box` with `style=\"rounded,filled\"`, the same look, because a record\n  shape makes Graphviz split the label at every `|` and a union type\n  (`unverified | self-reported`) came out as one field of three (measured\n  2026-10-09, caught by a browser test).\n- **A node is filled by its family.** The Form Documentor read colour schemes\n  from configuration; here the colour is the kind's family in `uml.css`, read\n  by `scripts/uml-palette.ts`, the one place a kind gets its colour. Owner:\n  *\"use existing themes for coloring\"*. No second palette.\n- **The layout is `unflatten`, then `dot`**, run by the viewer, not at build\n  time.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
